    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **51 tests, 0 failures/errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` as the human-formatted rendering of the stored E.164 `telephone`, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 added a public `display(String e164)` method (and made the class `public`) that renders a stored E.164 number as `'+' + country code`, a space, then the national digits grouped in threes. Country code is one digit for `+1` (NANP) and two otherwise \u2014 matching the codes this app normalizes to. So `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Returns `null` for absent or non-E.164 values (e.g. legacy seed data), so the field is simply omitted there.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `telephoneDisplay` to `E164Telephone.display(owner.getTelephone())`, consistent with how the other derived fields (`identityKey`, `locality`) reference helpers in the `function.owner` package.\n\nThe Cp37 test now confirms `$.telephone` = `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678` for input `0412 345 678`, and all 51 tests pass.",
